WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.835
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.105 --> 00:09.105
Honestly, I don't think your band can go on like this.

3
00:09.185 --> 00:11.425
What about that great guy you said you want in the band? What did he say?

4
00:11.505 --> 00:14.345
This time, he'll definitely say yes.

5
00:15.745 --> 00:17.225
You've cut yourself off from the outside world so much,

6
00:17.305 --> 00:19.145
you don't know what's going on out there.

7
00:19.225 --> 00:21.745
It's just one clip, but it has millions of views.

8
00:21.825 --> 00:24.985
Someone came to audition. He said his name was Phatee.

9
00:27.105 --> 00:29.105
I found your band's selling point.

10
00:29.185 --> 00:30.825
I agree to become a trainee

11
00:30.905 --> 00:32.224
and debut with your band.

12
00:32.305 --> 00:34.265
Thanks for doing this for our dream.

13
00:34.345 --> 00:36.025
Our band gets to keep going!

14
00:42.585 --> 00:43.665
P-ONE MUSIC LABEL - ARTIST CONTRACT

15
00:50.705 --> 00:52.185
Artist contract.

16
00:53.985 --> 00:56.065
According to the contract, the label's trainees

17
00:56.625 --> 00:58.385
can't take other jobs.

18
00:59.345 --> 01:00.465
Are you okay with that?

19
01:05.624 --> 01:07.105
Do whatever you want.

20
01:08.065 --> 01:09.825
I've never stopped you.

21
01:10.945 --> 01:12.385
Besides,

22
01:12.465 --> 01:14.865
you don't like taking jobs at the club anyway.

23
01:15.745 --> 01:17.745
Actually, becoming an artist is good too.

24
01:18.705 --> 01:21.585
If you become famous, I'll print your photo and put it up at the club,

25
01:21.665 --> 01:23.145
and tell everyone that I

26
01:23.225 --> 01:24.745
made you a star.

27
01:28.825 --> 01:29.665
Thank you.

28
01:30.265 --> 01:32.065
Then I'll hurry and move my stuff out.

29
01:33.105 --> 01:34.465
Why are you moving your stuff?

30
01:34.545 --> 01:36.465
Is your label making you live there?

31
01:37.265 --> 01:39.465
I don't work for you anymore.

32
01:39.545 --> 01:41.585
Do I still have the right to use the room?

33
01:44.145 --> 01:46.385
You know, becoming an artist takes time.

34
01:46.465 --> 01:48.505
To release a song,

35
01:48.585 --> 01:50.705
to get famous, to build a fanbase,

36
01:50.785 --> 01:52.465
it takes time.

37
01:55.465 --> 01:56.945
You don't have to move out.

38
01:57.025 --> 01:57.945
Stay here.

39
02:16.385 --> 02:17.745
You're not staying for free.

40
02:18.345 --> 02:20.545
I'll definitely charge you rent.

41
02:20.625 --> 02:22.305
I just haven't figured out yet

42
02:22.385 --> 02:24.345
how much to charge you.

43
02:43.825 --> 02:44.825
Enough.

44
02:46.145 --> 02:47.145
Enough.

45
02:50.385 --> 02:51.225
Thank you.

46
02:53.345 --> 02:55.745
Then I'll go practice.

47
03:08.145 --> 03:11.145
He's only a trainee, and you're already this happy.

48
03:11.225 --> 03:12.865
If he becomes an artist,

49
03:12.945 --> 03:15.545
won't you throw a three-day party for the whole block?

50
03:17.145 --> 03:18.745
Well, I'm proud of him.

51
03:18.825 --> 03:20.425
Who would've thought

52
03:20.505 --> 03:22.585
a broken-winged crow like Phatee

53
03:22.665 --> 03:24.785
would actually get to follow his real dream?

54
03:25.905 --> 03:29.145
When I went to Japan, you weren't this proud of me.

55
03:29.745 --> 03:30.625
Vann!

56
03:33.985 --> 03:35.225
Hey, Japan boy.

57
03:35.305 --> 03:36.625
You totally disappeared.

58
03:36.705 --> 03:38.265
I've been studying hard.

59
03:38.345 --> 03:39.505
Studying hard?

60
03:39.585 --> 03:41.785
If you're studying hard, how come you're here?

61
03:41.865 --> 03:42.825
Can I get another one?

62
03:42.905 --> 03:45.385
I really missed your nagging when I was in Japan.

63
03:45.465 --> 03:46.305
Stop.

64
03:47.505 --> 03:48.505
I'm not playing along.

65
03:51.065 --> 03:52.745
What? I didn't skip class.

66
03:52.825 --> 03:54.705
If you don't believe me, ask Rakkhun.

67
03:54.785 --> 03:55.905
Right, darling?

68
03:58.585 --> 04:01.265
It's a long holiday in Japan right now.

69
04:01.345 --> 04:02.905
So I booked him a ticket back.

70
04:04.145 --> 04:05.185
See?

71
04:05.705 --> 04:07.785
You two are really in sync.

72
04:09.825 --> 04:11.625
Whatever. I've given up.

73
04:11.705 --> 04:13.905
No matter what rules I make,

74
04:15.025 --> 04:17.545
none of the crows around here follow them.

75
04:18.545 --> 04:19.985
Just look at Talay.

76
04:21.265 --> 04:23.265
He's even seeing that writer guy.

77
04:24.385 --> 04:25.945
Hey, you.

78
04:26.025 --> 04:27.745
Why are you coming at me?

79
04:28.585 --> 04:30.025
It's just a temporary relationship.

80
04:30.105 --> 04:31.385
I'm not serious about it.

81
04:32.185 --> 04:33.665
Whatever.

82
04:35.065 --> 04:36.585
Every crow here

83
04:36.665 --> 04:38.265
is stubborn.

84
04:44.225 --> 04:45.465
Is this yours?

85
04:45.545 --> 04:48.705
SUN: IS THIS YOURS?

86
04:51.185 --> 04:52.425
You and that writer…

87
04:53.385 --> 04:54.265
Did it happen?

88
04:54.865 --> 04:55.665
What's with you?

89
04:55.745 --> 04:57.265
Stay out of it.

90
04:57.345 --> 04:59.145
Don't worry about me.

91
05:01.025 --> 05:02.425
And bring me a souvenir.

92
05:06.345 --> 05:07.425
Linda.

93
05:07.505 --> 05:08.665
Your souvenir.

94
05:10.465 --> 05:11.985
I'm charging you.

95
06:37.425 --> 06:39.865
I didn't think someone like you would bring me here.

96
06:43.145 --> 06:45.585
You wanted to know more about who I am, didn't you?

97
06:45.665 --> 06:47.665
What someone like me does all day.

98
06:48.705 --> 06:50.985
So you can use it as material for your novel.

99
07:08.425 --> 07:10.825
Did you really draw these yourself?

100
07:10.905 --> 07:12.945
You're not pretending to be an artist to fool me, are you?

101
07:19.065 --> 07:20.825
Want to try drawing one?

102
07:22.145 --> 07:23.585
I'm not good at drawing.

103
07:32.665 --> 07:34.585
Every drawing is beautiful.

104
07:35.465 --> 07:37.145
It depends on how you see it.

105
07:43.145 --> 07:44.705
If you don't want to draw,

106
07:46.425 --> 07:48.025
why don't you try writing something?

107
07:49.025 --> 07:50.345
You're a writer, aren't you?

108
08:25.865 --> 08:27.145
Virginia Woolf.

109
08:46.945 --> 08:48.625
Then draw me.

110
08:50.305 --> 08:51.305
No.

111
08:53.465 --> 08:54.985
I don't draw people.

112
08:56.665 --> 08:59.505
Why? Afraid it won't look good?

113
08:59.585 --> 09:01.785
With your brushwork,

114
09:01.865 --> 09:04.065
I think you could paint a cool portrait.

115
09:05.065 --> 09:06.545
I don't want to.

116
09:07.145 --> 09:10.145
What makes you think you can judge what's good or bad about me?

117
09:10.225 --> 09:12.425
I told you, you don't know me well.

118
09:13.225 --> 09:14.385
You see my face

119
09:14.465 --> 09:16.705
and judge me by my appearance like everyone else.

120
09:19.185 --> 09:22.265
Last night, I saw more than just your face.

121
09:32.625 --> 09:34.225
Did you leave anything else in my room?

122
09:48.025 --> 09:49.585
Next time, I definitely won't forget.

123
09:57.905 --> 09:59.665
There'll be a next time, right?

124
10:03.225 --> 10:04.465
Let me see how today goes first.

125
10:21.065 --> 10:22.505
Everyone,

126
10:23.065 --> 10:24.345
come here.

127
10:28.105 --> 10:30.225
Let's officially introduce ourselves again.

128
10:30.305 --> 10:31.785
This is Phatee.

129
10:32.465 --> 10:35.025
He'll be the main vocalist of A-team.

130
10:36.305 --> 10:39.185
And I have more good news for you.

131
10:39.265 --> 10:41.545
Your debut

132
10:42.145 --> 10:43.145
is in three months.

133
10:50.425 --> 10:51.985
Just do your best.

134
10:52.065 --> 10:54.425
And take care of Phatee.

135
10:55.225 --> 10:56.625
You can count on us.

136
11:01.425 --> 11:02.985
Finally! Guys,

137
11:03.065 --> 11:04.745
we're finally debuting!

138
11:05.505 --> 11:06.705
Hi.

139
11:06.785 --> 11:07.825
I'm PJ.

140
11:07.905 --> 11:10.265
I'm the keyboardist for A-team.

141
11:10.345 --> 11:11.625
Welcome.

142
11:13.385 --> 11:14.425
Okay.

143
11:16.665 --> 11:18.585
Hi. I'm Tonhon.

144
11:18.665 --> 11:20.545
I'm the bassist.

145
11:20.625 --> 11:21.785
And

146
11:21.865 --> 11:24.425
with a face this handsome, I'm the visual.

147
11:27.185 --> 11:28.465
Okay.

148
11:28.545 --> 11:30.305
Saw. I'm the drummer.

149
11:33.465 --> 11:35.625
Saw also produces.

150
11:35.705 --> 11:36.905
He can write songs.

151
11:36.985 --> 11:38.385
He can play guitar.

152
11:38.465 --> 11:39.545
You guys should hit it off.

153
11:43.785 --> 11:46.505
So, aren't you going to introduce yourself, big bro?

154
11:46.585 --> 11:48.665
How do you know I'm older?

155
11:48.745 --> 11:50.225
I could be younger than you.

156
11:52.105 --> 11:55.025
Kao told me you're the oldest in the band.

157
11:55.945 --> 11:57.585
So I figured you'd be older than me.

158
12:00.185 --> 12:01.185
That stings.

159
12:01.265 --> 12:02.945
Hey, man. Don't let it sting.

160
12:03.025 --> 12:05.785
Your face may look young,

161
12:05.865 --> 12:07.865
but you're the oldest in the whole building.

162
12:08.825 --> 12:10.105
Enough, Tonhon.

163
12:10.185 --> 12:12.305
All three of you

164
12:12.385 --> 12:13.865
are around the same age anyway.

165
12:19.025 --> 12:20.905
We finally get to formally introduce ourselves.

166
12:23.665 --> 12:24.705
I'm Ranne.

167
12:24.785 --> 12:26.105
I'm the main vocalist,

168
12:26.785 --> 12:27.905
guitarist,

169
12:27.985 --> 12:29.425
and band leader.

170
12:30.025 --> 12:31.465
Welcome, newbie.

171
12:36.065 --> 12:37.305
Glad to be joining you guys.

172
12:38.945 --> 12:42.185
From now on, just call me big bro,

173
12:42.265 --> 12:43.585
Phatee.

174
12:44.385 --> 12:45.985
So we can get close faster.

175
12:49.745 --> 12:50.585
Okay.

176
12:54.225 --> 12:55.145
Why are you guys smiling?

177
12:55.225 --> 12:56.065
Nothing, big bro.

178
12:56.145 --> 12:58.545
Come on, practice. It's time to practice.

179
12:58.625 --> 13:00.465
I'm debuting!

180
13:01.145 --> 13:02.585
START LIVESTREAM

181
13:02.665 --> 13:05.345
Today, we're practicing some basic dance moves.

182
13:07.745 --> 13:08.585
Come on.

183
13:08.665 --> 13:10.745
Today, we're practicing the basics.

184
13:10.825 --> 13:12.625
First move is a bounce. Bend down. Go.

185
13:12.705 --> 13:13.705
1.

186
13:14.465 --> 13:15.465
2.

187
13:16.025 --> 13:17.465
3. That's right.

188
13:17.545 --> 13:18.465
4.

189
13:18.545 --> 13:19.745
5.

190
13:19.825 --> 13:21.025
6.

191
13:21.105 --> 13:22.025
7.

192
13:22.105 --> 13:23.145
8, then back to 1.

193
13:23.225 --> 13:25.105
1, go. 2.

194
13:25.185 --> 13:26.785
3.

195
13:26.865 --> 13:28.265
4, come on.

196
13:28.345 --> 13:30.185
Now, for the second move, we'll use our legs.

197
13:30.265 --> 13:31.945
Start with your feet together.

198
13:32.025 --> 13:33.905
Step to the right, 1.

199
13:34.825 --> 13:35.745
2.

200
13:35.825 --> 13:37.345
Bring your right foot in.

201
13:37.425 --> 13:38.945
Then left foot, go.

202
13:39.625 --> 13:40.585
Back.

203
13:40.665 --> 13:42.545
Together. Forward.

204
13:43.265 --> 13:44.945
Together. Okay, faster now.

205
13:45.025 --> 13:47.145
5, 6, 7, 8. Go.

206
13:47.225 --> 13:49.225
1, 2, 3,

207
13:49.305 --> 13:51.305
4, 5, 6.

208
13:52.705 --> 13:53.785
Sorry.

209
13:56.665 --> 13:57.545
Everyone, take a break.

210
13:58.345 --> 13:59.465
Except you.

211
14:00.465 --> 14:01.465
Keep practicing.

212
14:03.225 --> 14:04.225
Come on.

213
14:06.785 --> 14:08.145
Let's work on your footwork. Again.

214
14:08.225 --> 14:09.985
Start. 1.

215
14:10.785 --> 14:12.385
Right. 2.

216
14:13.145 --> 14:14.385
Back. Left.

217
14:15.625 --> 14:17.185
Bring your right foot in. 3.

218
14:18.065 --> 14:19.185
Right.

219
14:19.265 --> 14:20.345
Then bend down a little.

220
14:20.865 --> 14:22.505
Then your left foot forward. 4.

221
14:23.545 --> 14:25.105
Right. Bring this foot in.

222
14:25.185 --> 14:26.385
Right, cross.

223
14:26.465 --> 14:27.425
5.

224
14:28.185 --> 14:29.465
Bring it in. 6.

225
14:30.105 --> 14:31.145
Step forward. 7.

226
14:31.785 --> 14:32.745
Bring your foot in. 8.

227
14:35.145 --> 14:36.585
Can he handle it?

228
14:39.065 --> 14:40.185
It's only his first day.

229
14:41.465 --> 14:43.385
Shouldn't he have some basics down?

230
14:44.105 --> 14:45.865
You guys were like this on your first day too.

231
14:47.545 --> 14:48.545
7.

232
14:49.145 --> 14:50.185
8.

233
14:53.585 --> 14:54.985
Damn it.

234
14:55.065 --> 14:56.625
I thought we'd finally get to debut.

235
14:57.225 --> 14:59.105
Now I'm starting to stress out.

236
14:59.705 --> 15:01.625
Damn, I thought he'd have some basics down.

237
15:01.705 --> 15:03.505
He's clearly below zero.

238
15:04.665 --> 15:06.065
You guys.

239
15:06.145 --> 15:07.145
Go back and practice.

240
15:09.105 --> 15:11.025
I just came out for some fresh air.

241
15:11.105 --> 15:12.945
The air inside was so damn stuffy.

242
15:23.865 --> 15:25.105
Don't overthink it.

243
15:26.025 --> 15:27.705
I was way worse on my first day.

244
15:29.665 --> 15:31.025
I really can't dance.

245
15:31.585 --> 15:32.745
You don't have to comfort me.

246
15:33.265 --> 15:36.185
I'm not comforting you. I'm serious.

247
15:36.705 --> 15:39.225
It took me a long time to get this good at dancing.

248
15:39.825 --> 15:41.185
It's only your first day.

249
15:41.265 --> 15:42.345
Don't worry.

250
15:43.185 --> 15:44.545
You can do it.

251
15:51.545 --> 15:52.545
How about this?

252
15:53.185 --> 15:56.225
I'll help teach you to dance.

253
15:56.305 --> 15:57.345
Okay?

254
15:58.825 --> 16:00.825
I don't want to trouble you, Ranne.

255
16:03.345 --> 16:05.065
We're in the same boat now.

256
16:05.145 --> 16:06.905
We have to help each other make it to shore.

257
16:08.545 --> 16:09.545
Besides,

258
16:09.625 --> 16:11.145
I told you to call me big bro.

259
16:12.065 --> 16:13.505
Don't let me hear you

260
16:13.585 --> 16:14.785
calling me just Ranne again.

261
16:14.865 --> 16:16.265
It sounds distant.

262
16:25.705 --> 16:26.985
Are you touched?

263
16:28.745 --> 16:29.745
No.

264
16:30.465 --> 16:31.825
If I call you big bro,

265
16:32.545 --> 16:33.505
you'll sound too old.

266
16:35.345 --> 16:36.505
You little brat.

267
16:37.865 --> 16:39.385
I was being serious.

268
16:45.985 --> 16:51.265
Do… Re…

269
16:52.225 --> 16:55.265
Mi…

270
16:55.345 --> 16:57.625
Go. 1, 2, 3, 4.

271
16:57.705 --> 16:59.705
5, 6, 7, 8. Go.

272
16:59.785 --> 17:01.745
2, 2, 3, 4.

273
17:01.825 --> 17:03.825
5, 6, 7, 8. Go.

274
17:03.905 --> 17:05.585
3, 2, 3, 4.

275
17:05.665 --> 17:07.825
5, 6, 7, 8.

276
17:07.905 --> 17:09.825
4, 2, 3, 4.

277
17:09.905 --> 17:11.505
5, 6, 7, 8.

278
17:11.585 --> 17:12.625
Feel it here.

279
17:13.704 --> 17:15.385
Then push it down.

280
17:16.105 --> 17:17.704
Bring it down first.

281
17:17.785 --> 17:19.305
Then bring it out.

282
17:20.224 --> 17:21.505
Then down again.

283
17:22.065 --> 17:23.905
Go as deep as you can.

284
17:29.585 --> 17:32.905
Come look at this.

285
17:32.985 --> 17:34.585
How about a lower key?

286
17:35.265 --> 17:36.745
You mean lower the key?

287
17:36.825 --> 17:38.105
Here, let me show you.

288
17:38.185 --> 17:40.905
I'll teach you. Here, like this.

289
17:41.585 --> 17:42.985
Sweep your hand down like this.

290
17:43.065 --> 17:46.185
Then sweep your hand past your face like this.

291
17:48.385 --> 17:49.385
Is this enough?

292
17:50.425 --> 17:52.185
Yes. Turn your face that way.

293
17:58.265 --> 17:59.265
Phatee.

294
17:59.345 --> 18:00.425
Okay.

295
18:01.465 --> 18:04.025
‎Do…

296
18:06.065 --> 18:08.825
Re…

297
19:11.505 --> 19:12.625
Thanks.

298
19:20.705 --> 19:21.665
This works.

299
19:22.705 --> 19:23.705
Oh.

300
19:25.145 --> 19:28.225
Lately, we've been practicing late every night.

301
19:28.305 --> 19:30.105
Thanks for putting in the effort.

302
19:31.585 --> 19:33.105
You're doing things you're not good at,

303
19:34.185 --> 19:36.745
and you have to adjust to the other members too.

304
19:37.825 --> 19:40.465
I know the first step is always hard.

305
19:41.305 --> 19:43.185
But I'll stay by your side

306
19:43.265 --> 19:44.785
and keep pushing you forward.

307
19:47.225 --> 19:49.505
I'm here because of you.

308
19:50.425 --> 19:52.585
You've always been my inspiration.

309
20:00.385 --> 20:01.505
Hold on.

310
20:04.785 --> 20:05.945
Okay.

311
20:06.025 --> 20:07.745
What you just said was…

312
20:08.545 --> 20:09.545
for content?

313
20:10.785 --> 20:12.025
Yeah.

314
20:12.105 --> 20:14.305
We have to make content for the label's channel too.

315
20:15.145 --> 20:16.345
Right now,

316
20:16.425 --> 20:18.185
we're in the pre-debut phase, right?

317
20:18.265 --> 20:19.705
It helps attract fans.

318
20:20.625 --> 20:23.145
Besides, it's the label's promo plan.

319
20:23.945 --> 20:25.225
Didn't Kao tell you?

320
20:29.025 --> 20:31.625
Or… did it look fake? We can do another take.

321
20:31.705 --> 20:32.905
No.

322
20:33.505 --> 20:35.145
I think that was…

323
20:35.225 --> 20:36.385
fine.

324
20:36.465 --> 20:38.545
If we shoot it again, it'll look fake.

325
20:42.465 --> 20:43.665
Oh, and,

326
20:44.305 --> 20:45.505
you just said

327
20:45.585 --> 20:47.825
I've always been your inspiration.

328
20:48.945 --> 20:50.265
Did you know me before?

329
20:54.505 --> 20:56.145
I was just saying stuff.

330
20:57.385 --> 20:58.745
Really?

331
20:58.825 --> 20:59.785
But you don't seem

332
20:59.865 --> 21:01.505
like someone who just says stuff.

333
21:04.665 --> 21:05.825
Well…

334
21:07.545 --> 21:08.785
it's for content.

335
21:09.385 --> 21:10.385
I've been practicing.

336
21:11.665 --> 21:12.825
Very good.

337
21:12.905 --> 21:13.825
From now on,

338
21:13.905 --> 21:16.305
the two of us have to make content together.

339
21:17.265 --> 21:18.425
So from now on,

340
21:19.345 --> 21:20.265
when you see a camera,

341
21:20.345 --> 21:21.665
give it a smile.

342
21:21.745 --> 21:22.745
Okay?

343
21:24.225 --> 21:25.225
Okay.

344
21:25.745 --> 21:26.705
Come on, smile.

345
21:28.585 --> 21:29.705
Come on, smile.

346
21:30.745 --> 21:32.145
Come on, smile.

347
21:33.545 --> 21:34.545
Show your teeth too.

348
22:11.345 --> 22:12.345
Let's keep eating.

349
22:27.625 --> 22:28.745
Look at this, guys.

350
22:42.745 --> 22:44.185
No joke.

351
22:44.265 --> 22:45.625
I think

352
22:45.705 --> 22:46.985
since Phatee joined,

353
22:47.065 --> 22:49.705
our band's engagement has shot way up.

354
22:49.785 --> 22:51.705
I'm starting to love Phatee.

355
22:51.785 --> 22:53.505
At first, I saw he couldn't really dance.

356
22:53.585 --> 22:55.385
Turns out, people really are

357
22:55.465 --> 22:56.825
good at different things.

358
22:56.905 --> 22:59.345
Phatee really is talented.

359
22:59.425 --> 23:01.625
It's not just about pulling in views.

360
23:01.705 --> 23:02.745
Look over there.

361
23:08.185 --> 23:09.105
Take a look.

362
23:15.025 --> 23:16.465
He's even better than me.

363
23:18.945 --> 23:21.265
Let's cut the rap. It's too much. It won't have that wow factor.

364
23:22.425 --> 23:23.465
Let's do it.

365
23:23.545 --> 23:26.145
Something like this. Take a look.

366
23:28.185 --> 23:29.425
Whoa.

367
23:29.505 --> 23:30.425
It's really good.

368
23:30.505 --> 23:31.905
Hey, everyone.

369
23:31.985 --> 23:32.905
Phatee's old song,

370
23:32.985 --> 23:34.545
with a new arrangement,

371
23:34.625 --> 23:36.105
is finished!

372
23:36.185 --> 23:37.625
-Come here. -Let me see.

373
23:37.705 --> 23:38.785
Come check it out.

374
23:40.425 --> 23:41.665
Let's see.

375
23:41.745 --> 23:42.825
Check this out.

376
23:47.185 --> 23:49.265
-Whoa. -Shit!

377
23:50.425 --> 23:51.865
He can compose this well?

378
23:51.945 --> 23:53.545
This is the real deal.

379
23:53.625 --> 23:55.145
It's not that hard.

380
23:55.225 --> 23:57.185
Hey, you could be a little humble.

381
23:59.425 --> 24:02.065
How about we

382
24:02.145 --> 24:03.265
try playing it?

383
24:03.905 --> 24:05.185
-Let's do it. -Let's try it.

384
24:05.265 --> 24:07.105
-We're trying it now? -Yeah, let's try it now.

385
24:07.185 --> 24:09.265
-Hey, what are you afraid of? -We won't know until we try.

386
24:09.345 --> 24:10.545
Okay, come on.

387
24:10.625 --> 24:12.345
-Do you remember the chords? -I do.

388
24:12.425 --> 24:13.265
Let's do it.

389
25:44.585 --> 25:45.745
Whose song is this?

390
25:49.665 --> 25:50.745
Well…

391
25:50.825 --> 25:53.025
It's an old song of Phatee's

392
25:53.105 --> 25:54.665
that we rearranged.

393
26:02.665 --> 26:05.745
Okay. Good. Let's make this your debut song.

394
26:06.825 --> 26:07.825
Really?

395
26:07.905 --> 26:09.185
Really.

396
26:09.265 --> 26:10.745
It's your time now.

397
26:10.825 --> 26:12.985
You can start recording the song,

398
26:13.065 --> 26:15.385
planning the promotion, and shooting the MV.

399
26:15.465 --> 26:17.425
You don't have to wait three months anymore.

400
26:17.505 --> 26:18.825
If you're ready, just debut.

401
26:21.505 --> 26:22.785
We're finally debuting!

402
26:22.865 --> 26:24.865
We did it!

403
26:25.665 --> 26:27.345
-Thank you. -Thank you.

404
26:30.265 --> 26:34.665
Thanks, Phatee. It's all because of you that our band has come this far.

405
26:35.465 --> 26:37.265
It's not that big a deal.

406
26:39.465 --> 26:40.745
Come on, be happy.

407
26:40.825 --> 26:42.265
Come on, after everything you've done.

408
26:44.545 --> 26:47.345
We did it!

409
27:01.785 --> 27:03.225
Why are you back so early today?

410
27:06.385 --> 27:08.545
It's already 2 a.m.

411
27:10.065 --> 27:12.025
You usually get back at 3 or 4 a.m.

412
27:12.785 --> 27:14.945
So? Is being a trainee fun?

413
27:16.665 --> 27:17.785
It's not bad.

414
27:26.705 --> 27:28.025
If you want to talk, go ahead.

415
27:28.105 --> 27:30.425
If not, have a drink with me.

416
27:41.865 --> 27:43.745
I've seen your clips all over social media.

417
27:43.825 --> 27:45.225
You're getting a lot of buzz.

418
27:45.305 --> 27:47.825
People are even shipping you with Ranne.

419
27:49.025 --> 27:50.785
He's the one who kept pursuing you at the club, right?

420
27:53.145 --> 27:54.345
It's just content.

421
27:55.585 --> 27:58.025
Why? You don't like it?

422
27:59.425 --> 28:00.945
I don't know either.

423
28:01.025 --> 28:02.385
I don't know if

424
28:02.465 --> 28:04.305
Ranne is nice to me

425
28:04.385 --> 28:06.425
because he genuinely wants to be,

426
28:07.465 --> 28:08.465
or because…

427
28:09.665 --> 28:11.065
we just have to work together.

428
28:13.025 --> 28:14.585
I thought it was something serious.

429
28:15.345 --> 28:16.665
So it's a matter of the heart.

430
28:19.665 --> 28:21.065
What would you do?

431
28:21.945 --> 28:23.305
I wouldn't care

432
28:23.385 --> 28:25.225
whether he's doing it for work

433
28:25.305 --> 28:26.825
or because of personal feelings.

434
28:27.865 --> 28:29.665
I'd make the most of it.

435
28:30.265 --> 28:31.825
It's like dreaming.

436
28:31.905 --> 28:33.665
You know you'll have to wake up,

437
28:33.745 --> 28:35.185
but so what?

438
28:35.265 --> 28:36.785
Just dreaming makes you happy, right?

439
28:37.465 --> 28:39.225
What if I wake up from the dream?

440
28:39.745 --> 28:41.185
Then you have two choices.

441
28:41.265 --> 28:42.985
Go back to sleep

442
28:43.505 --> 28:45.425
and hope you have the same good dream again.

443
28:45.505 --> 28:46.905
Or

444
28:46.985 --> 28:49.185
make your dream a reality.

445
29:11.465 --> 29:12.945
Scrub harder.

446
29:13.025 --> 29:14.225
Do you have any strength?

447
29:20.025 --> 29:20.945
Like this.

448
29:22.025 --> 29:22.985
Like this.

449
29:24.705 --> 29:26.985
You're still as strong as ever.

450
29:28.505 --> 29:30.425
You should eat more.

451
29:30.505 --> 29:32.025
You're so skinny.

452
29:32.105 --> 29:34.025
One puff and you'd blow away.

453
29:38.465 --> 29:39.625
Oh.

454
29:39.705 --> 29:41.985
You're Tangmo's ex.

455
29:42.065 --> 29:43.425
You're at The Crow Club now?

456
29:44.345 --> 29:45.625
Or did you two get back together?

457
29:45.705 --> 29:48.785
Stop it, Vann. Want a smack?

458
29:48.865 --> 29:49.865
I just…

459
29:51.105 --> 29:52.985
hired him to clean.

460
29:53.065 --> 29:54.985
I'm lazy.

461
29:55.065 --> 29:56.025
That's all.

462
29:57.665 --> 30:00.145
But it looks like you're the one cleaning.

463
30:03.505 --> 30:06.025
Keep scrubbing. Make sure it's clean.

464
30:06.105 --> 30:07.825
Then go scrub the bathroom too.

465
30:13.585 --> 30:14.825
Don't panic.

466
30:15.985 --> 30:17.865
The more you panic, the more suspicious you look.

467
30:18.865 --> 30:20.185
Even if there's nothing,

468
30:21.145 --> 30:23.105
people will think there is.

469
30:57.105 --> 30:58.265
What's this?

470
30:59.585 --> 31:00.985
It's your debut song.

471
31:01.705 --> 31:03.185
What did you do to it?

472
31:03.265 --> 31:04.705
The original was already good.

473
31:05.425 --> 31:08.585
I tried having AI polish it. I didn't do anything.

474
31:09.425 --> 31:10.825
You used AI?

475
31:10.905 --> 31:11.985
Saw.

476
31:13.305 --> 31:15.305
There are plenty of producers at your label.

477
31:15.385 --> 31:16.825
I can do it too.

478
31:16.905 --> 31:18.785
I didn't use AI for everything.

479
31:18.865 --> 31:20.145
Just to polish it up.

480
31:20.225 --> 31:21.785
What the fuck do you mean you didn't?

481
31:21.865 --> 31:23.625
You changed almost the whole song.

482
31:23.705 --> 31:25.785
What's the point of art if you do this?

483
31:25.865 --> 31:27.145
So what do you want?

484
31:27.225 --> 31:28.945
If you're debuting with this song,

485
31:29.025 --> 31:30.345
then they can debut as four.

486
31:30.425 --> 31:31.785
-I'm out. -Hey.

487
31:31.865 --> 31:32.905
Saw.

488
31:32.985 --> 31:34.105
Don't say that, Saw.

489
31:34.185 --> 31:36.185
If the label owner wants to use AI,

490
31:36.265 --> 31:38.665
why not use AI to create an artist?

491
31:38.745 --> 31:40.385
That seems more your style.

492
31:41.425 --> 31:43.545
-Saw. -Saw.

493
31:43.625 --> 31:44.905
-Fuck. -What's his problem?

494
31:44.985 --> 31:47.185
He's making such a big deal out of this.

495
31:47.265 --> 31:49.225
But I think this band will make it anyway

496
31:49.305 --> 31:51.385
with Phatee and Ranne.

497
31:51.465 --> 31:55.145
They're both getting a lot of buzz right now.

498
31:56.025 --> 31:57.625
What do you guys think?

499
31:57.705 --> 31:59.465
If you continue without Saw?

500
32:00.585 --> 32:02.185
If we had a choice,

501
32:02.265 --> 32:03.945
we'd rather debut as five.

502
32:04.625 --> 32:07.585
Then I'll give you three days.

503
32:07.665 --> 32:09.385
Think it over.

504
32:09.465 --> 32:11.265
If Saw doesn't come back,

505
32:11.345 --> 32:12.625
what are you going to do?

506
32:30.265 --> 32:31.385
What the hell?

507
32:58.545 --> 33:00.785
You could call him a hundred times. He won't answer.

508
33:00.865 --> 33:02.545
When he's ready, he'll come talk to you.

509
33:04.265 --> 33:05.505
So what are you going to do

510
33:05.585 --> 33:06.985
if he quits?

511
33:07.625 --> 33:09.705
Everything's been set for five people,

512
33:09.785 --> 33:11.905
both the blocking and vocal parts.

513
33:11.985 --> 33:13.585
I'm not giving up that easily.

514
33:14.505 --> 33:15.985
You guys go home for today.

515
33:16.905 --> 33:18.265
I'll handle Saw myself.

516
33:20.305 --> 33:21.545
Keep us posted.

517
33:38.345 --> 33:41.225
Why haven't you left yet?

518
33:42.785 --> 33:43.985
You looked stressed,

519
33:44.865 --> 33:46.145
so I'm staying with you.

520
33:49.745 --> 33:51.305
Let's call it a day.

521
33:51.825 --> 33:53.025
I'll take you home.

522
33:54.265 --> 33:56.625
Isn't it in the opposite direction for you?

523
33:59.265 --> 34:00.265
It's fine.

524
34:00.985 --> 34:02.905
I was going to see Saw too.

525
34:04.265 --> 34:05.825
Then I'll come with you.

526
34:17.344 --> 34:19.304
Can you open it for me?

527
34:29.945 --> 34:32.705
Saw must've known I was coming.

528
34:32.784 --> 34:34.385
That's why he hasn't come back.

529
34:34.465 --> 34:36.344
He's not posting on social media.

530
34:37.145 --> 34:38.505
He won't reply to my texts either.

531
34:42.225 --> 34:43.945
You probably need to give him some time.

532
34:44.025 --> 34:46.025
Where on earth is he?

533
34:46.945 --> 34:48.545
He doesn't have many friends.

534
34:51.304 --> 34:52.945
Or…

535
34:53.025 --> 34:54.945
maybe he went back to his parents.

536
34:55.545 --> 34:57.625
Or he's staying with a sibling for a while.

537
35:00.025 --> 35:01.225
Right.

538
35:01.305 --> 35:02.985
Saw has an older sister.

539
35:03.945 --> 35:06.225
But I messaged her, and she hasn't replied yet.

540
35:07.385 --> 35:10.025
I don't know where his parents live either.

541
35:11.025 --> 35:12.545
But he could be there.

542
35:14.585 --> 35:17.185
Then wait for his sister to reply first.

543
35:17.265 --> 35:19.265
Then figure out what to do.

544
35:23.225 --> 35:24.225
You know,

545
35:26.065 --> 35:28.625
we've given up on this dream so many times.

546
35:30.545 --> 35:31.865
We're so close.

547
35:33.065 --> 35:34.465
We're really so close.

548
35:36.305 --> 35:38.185
We have to debut as five.

549
36:04.305 --> 36:05.825
Thanks.

550
36:09.625 --> 36:11.265
Aren't you practicing with the band today?

551
36:12.225 --> 36:13.585
Not today.

552
36:17.065 --> 36:19.185
Have you ever taken a job finding someone?

553
36:19.265 --> 36:20.905
Not often.

554
36:20.985 --> 36:23.305
Linda usually gives jobs like that to Mimi.

555
36:24.185 --> 36:27.305
She's an expert at catching cheaters and finding missing people.

556
36:27.385 --> 36:29.385
Missing dogs and cats too. That's her specialty.

557
36:30.265 --> 36:31.185
Why?

558
36:31.705 --> 36:33.945
Someone in my band had a fight with the label,

559
36:34.025 --> 36:35.225
and then he disappeared.

560
36:36.545 --> 36:37.825
What's that got to do with you?

561
36:39.305 --> 36:40.425
Well…

562
36:40.505 --> 36:43.465
it has nothing to do with me. But it has to do with Ranne.

563
36:47.105 --> 36:48.505
Heart trouble again.

564
36:52.745 --> 36:53.665
Yeah.

565
36:55.985 --> 36:57.665
Is Mimi here?

566
36:58.505 --> 37:00.065
Mimi's not here.

567
37:08.105 --> 37:09.065
Let me see.

568
37:09.145 --> 37:11.545
Who are you looking for?

569
37:18.625 --> 37:20.025
His name is Saw.

570
37:20.105 --> 37:22.905
He might be hard to find because he rarely posts anything.

571
37:23.505 --> 37:24.865
Saw.

572
37:33.265 --> 37:34.985
Do you believe in fate?

573
37:36.865 --> 37:37.865
What's with you?

574
37:37.945 --> 37:39.905
Are you picking someone based on a profile picture?

575
37:40.825 --> 37:42.145
No!

576
37:42.665 --> 37:44.705
Linda just told me about a job where I'd pretend

577
37:44.785 --> 37:46.985
to be someone's boyfriend to fool her family.

578
37:47.065 --> 37:49.105
And the person who contacted us…

579
37:50.585 --> 37:51.625
is this girl.

580
37:53.585 --> 37:54.545
When?

581
37:55.225 --> 37:56.305
This afternoon.

582
38:11.385 --> 38:14.225
With you two staring like that, my boyfriend's getting nervous.

583
38:15.665 --> 38:17.585
Your name is Sky, right?

584
38:18.545 --> 38:19.465
Yes.

585
38:19.545 --> 38:21.345
What do you do?

586
38:24.065 --> 38:26.185
I'm an engineer.

587
38:26.265 --> 38:27.305
I work for a construction company.

588
38:29.025 --> 38:30.705
Good career.

589
38:30.785 --> 38:31.945
Good-looking too.

590
38:32.025 --> 38:33.665
I like this one.

591
38:33.745 --> 38:35.745
I don't want another one like your ex.

592
38:35.825 --> 38:37.025
I know.

593
38:37.625 --> 38:39.585
Where do you live?

594
38:41.185 --> 38:42.465
I live in Lat Phrao.

595
38:42.545 --> 38:44.305
Is it a condo or a townhouse?

596
38:45.625 --> 38:46.785
-Mom. -It's a condo.

597
38:46.865 --> 38:48.865
How did you get here? What car did you drive?

598
38:48.945 --> 38:50.105
Dad.

599
38:50.705 --> 38:51.625
I took a Grab.

600
38:51.705 --> 38:53.905
Oh, so you don't have to worry about parking.

601
38:55.785 --> 38:57.225
There he is.

602
39:00.825 --> 39:02.465
How did you get here?

603
39:07.705 --> 39:10.625
You know your sister's boyfriend too?

604
39:10.705 --> 39:11.945
Boyfriend?

605
39:13.505 --> 39:14.625
Yes.

606
39:14.705 --> 39:16.585
This is Sky, my boyfriend.

607
39:16.665 --> 39:18.385
How would you know my boyfriend?

608
39:23.785 --> 39:25.745
Maybe I mistook him for someone else.

609
39:26.785 --> 39:27.945
Okay, okay.

610
39:28.025 --> 39:29.905
Come on, let's eat.

611
39:29.985 --> 39:31.665
You must all be starving.

612
39:33.345 --> 39:36.225
-Eat a lot so you'll grow. -Okay.

613
39:51.185 --> 39:52.305
Ranne.

614
39:52.905 --> 39:55.745
Ranne, can I take a photo with you?

615
39:55.825 --> 39:56.945
Sure.

616
40:00.905 --> 40:02.505
Thank you.

617
40:12.425 --> 40:13.705
Excuse me.

618
40:13.785 --> 40:15.145
Is Phatee here?

619
40:15.225 --> 40:17.145
I haven't been able to reach him all day.

620
40:17.225 --> 40:18.345
I was wondering who it was.

621
40:18.425 --> 40:19.745
It's Phatee's ship partner.

622
40:19.825 --> 40:21.985
Phatee's not here. He's working.

623
40:22.065 --> 40:23.585
But he'll be back soon.

624
40:24.145 --> 40:26.465
Then I'll wait here.

625
40:29.785 --> 40:32.145
I don't think it's good to stay here. There's no privacy.

626
40:32.225 --> 40:34.225
Want to go to Phatee's room? I'll take you.

627
40:35.825 --> 40:38.625
-Okay. Sorry to trouble you. -He's so handsome.

628
40:38.705 --> 40:40.505
We have to tell our friends.

629
40:40.585 --> 40:42.625
Post it in the group.

630
40:44.345 --> 40:46.785
-I'll share it with my friends on IG. -Drinks are here.

631
40:47.305 --> 40:48.145
Thanks.

632
40:55.465 --> 40:57.185
That scared me.

633
41:03.065 --> 41:04.665
I haven't seen you for a while,

634
41:04.745 --> 41:05.785
and you already changed your name.

635
41:08.745 --> 41:10.585
And now you're my sister's boyfriend.

636
41:12.625 --> 41:14.105
If I didn't do this,

637
41:14.945 --> 41:16.345
would I get to see you?

638
41:18.265 --> 41:20.465
Ranne and everyone are really worried about you.

639
41:21.905 --> 41:23.625
Are you really leaving the band this easily?

640
41:27.305 --> 41:29.065
Would you dare sing that AI song?

641
41:30.745 --> 41:32.545
Just go talk to Kao.

642
41:37.625 --> 41:38.985
Kao won't listen to me.

643
41:40.705 --> 41:42.065
She doesn't care about anyone

644
41:43.345 --> 41:44.705
except you and Ranne.

645
41:47.185 --> 41:48.385
What's with you?

646
41:51.425 --> 41:52.785
You really don't know?

647
41:53.825 --> 41:55.385
You only get to debut

648
41:56.425 --> 41:58.225
because they're selling your ship with Ranne.

649
42:04.145 --> 42:05.665
How do you know?

650
42:07.025 --> 42:08.585
It might not be that serious.

651
42:09.465 --> 42:11.065
How could I not know?

652
42:12.785 --> 42:14.745
Ranne just didn't want me to tell you.

653
42:14.825 --> 42:15.865
And now,

654
42:16.625 --> 42:19.145
you and Ranne are getting lots of jobs together.

655
42:20.545 --> 42:23.265
But Ranne told Kao he wants to take them after debut.

656
42:24.705 --> 42:26.065
Otherwise, you'd feel pressured

657
42:27.105 --> 42:28.705
and turn down the jobs.

658
42:31.225 --> 42:32.705
That's why Kao wants you to debut soon.

659
42:37.185 --> 42:38.465
But I went along with it

660
42:40.585 --> 42:43.145
because at least I'd get closer to my dream.

661
42:45.905 --> 42:47.745
But now I guess Kao doesn't even see me anymore.

662
42:49.145 --> 42:50.985
So I don't know why I should stay.

663
42:56.665 --> 42:58.905
What if I get them to stop using AI

664
43:00.225 --> 43:01.625
and use the song you wrote?

665
43:03.265 --> 43:04.305
Will you come back?

666
43:07.705 --> 43:08.985
Without me,

667
43:09.905 --> 43:11.185
you can still debut.

668
43:12.865 --> 43:13.905
I'm not important.

669
43:15.745 --> 43:17.025
That's not true.

670
43:18.065 --> 43:19.185
You are important.

671
44:20.385 --> 44:22.745
SONGBOOK

672
45:02.185 --> 45:03.665
RANNE

673
45:05.625 --> 45:08.105
-I'm putting mine here. -I'll stick mine here.

674
45:08.185 --> 45:09.705
I really like you.

675
45:09.785 --> 45:12.865
-Thank you. -Ranne, I'm putting mine here.

676
45:13.465 --> 45:15.745
Happy Valentine's Day.

677
45:16.785 --> 45:18.625
There's Phatee. Come on.

678
45:18.705 --> 45:21.065
-Phatee! -Phatee!

679
45:27.145 --> 45:28.745
I really like you.

680
45:30.345 --> 45:33.745
RANNE

681
46:24.505 --> 46:25.905
So what's going on with you and Phatee?

682
46:25.985 --> 46:28.985
The way he looks at you is nothing like how he looks at anyone else.

683
46:29.065 --> 46:31.985
-Do you like me? -The opportunity is here.

684
46:32.065 --> 46:32.945
You have to seize it.

685
46:33.025 --> 46:34.585
Which one do you mean?

686
46:34.665 --> 46:36.585
Both your dream and your love life.

687
46:36.665 --> 46:38.305
Come on, let's go see Phatee.

688
46:38.385 --> 46:40.425
Why did you bring me here? It's crowded.

689
46:40.505 --> 46:42.025
Then just keep looking at me like this.

690
46:42.105 --> 46:44.065
Did you trick me into looking at you?

691
46:44.145 --> 46:48.345
Close your eyes and think about what you want to happen.

692
46:48.425 --> 46:49.425
You can open your eyes now.
